{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p \\\"/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/runs/run-20260426T203933Z--skkq4u3p1p/semantic/comment_section_generation\\\" && cat > \\\"/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/runs/run-20260426T203933Z--skkq4u3p1p/semantic/comment_section_generation/source--source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c.json\\\" <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"page_ref\\\": \\\"source:source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\\\",\n  \\\"requested_count\\\": 5,\n  \\\"comments\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-1\\\",\n      \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-maya-santoro\\\",\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"What I like about this approach is that the skeleton is not just a visual metaphor. By inflating each edge cluster into a shape, the method gives itself a geometric object whose centerline really can guide the bundled edges while keeping node positions fixed.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": null,\n      \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n        \\\"score\\\": 22,\n        \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Grounded in the source's core skeleton and endpoint-preserving mechanics, with a clear interpretive point.\\\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-2\\\",\n      \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-eli-okafor\\\",\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"The repeated reclustering step feels crucial. A single global clustering pass would probably make the usual hairball look tidier, but the progressive thresholds explain why the paper can form smaller reliable bundles before allowing them to merge into larger routes.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": null,\n      \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n        \\\"score\\\": 20,\n        \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Accurately highlights progressive bundling and explains its value without overstating the result.\\\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-3\\\",\n      \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-lina-kovac\\\",\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"The warning about information loss should not be treated as a footnote. These views are useful for seeing coarse corridors, but once individual edge identity and exact direction are obscured, the visualization needs to be paired with interaction or filtering for detailed analysis.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": null,\n      \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n        \\\"score\\\": 24,\n        \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Strongly grounded in the paper's stated limitations and adds a practical analysis implication.\\\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-4\\\",\n      \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-rory-chen\\\",\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"Agreed, and that limitation is partly why the cushion shading and smoothing controls matter. They do not recover the lost topology, but they can make overlapping bundles easier to follow when the goal is overview rather than exact path tracing.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"draft-3\\\",\n      \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n        \\\"score\\\": 18,\n        \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Relevant reply that connects visual controls to the thread's limitation point, though less detailed than the root comment.\\\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-5\\\",\n      \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-samira-haddad\\\",\n      \\\"body\\\": \\\"The GPU-heavy framing also seems important for judging the contribution. Distance transforms, skeletonization, path selection, and attraction are all image-space operations here, so the reported seconds-scale runtimes are tied to that implementation choice rather than just the abstract bundling idea.\\\",\n      \\\"parent_ref\\\": null,\n      \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n        \\\"score\\\": 21,\n        \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Well aligned with the implementation and performance evidence, with a careful qualification about runtime claims.\\\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
